    card title "Nature's draw"

The best-studied gene for dri (@draw aldh@)nking makes an enzyme called ALDH2, which does the second of the two steps in which your body breaks alcohol down.

A common variant of its gene, call it (@draw legA@) A, cuts that enzyme's activity sharply, and two copies all but switch it off; the (@draw legG@) usual version we will call G.

With an A on board, a toxic by-product, acetaldehyde, pile (@draw flushicon@)s up after a drink: the face flushes, the heart races, nausea follows.

So carriers drink less, and people with two copies drink very little; the  (@highlight legA2@)variant is common in East Asia and rare elsewhere.
    draw legA2

Now take a mother and a father who each carry one G and one A.
    draw par_f par_m

Each passes on one of their two copies, and which one is set (@draw h_mG h_mA@)tled by chance when the egg or the sperm is made.
    draw h_fG h_fA

So every child of theirs lands in one of these four cells, each with probability one quarter.
    draw grid cells

    quiz "These parents have many children. What share of them will carry at least one A?" intro "Before the count."
        right: Three in four: every cell but the top-left GG holds an A.
        wrong: Count the cells that hold at least one A, not only the AA cell.
        * One in four
        * One in two
        + Three in four

    erase legG legA legA2 flushicon aldh

Three cells of four hold an A, so three children in four will flush, and one in four will be free to drink.
    draw sh_1 sh_2 sh_3 share parallel true

That is why an allele is closer to a lottery draw than almost anything an economist can find.
    highlight g_out

The draw is made at conception, before income, smoking or any illne (@highlight h_fA h_mA@)ss exists, so none of them could have set it.
    draw conc

And nothing that happens later, no habit and no disease, can reach back and change which cell a child is in.
    point at.ref c_GG gesture circle

But the draw is fair only among the children of the same parents.
    focus par_f par_m

Across a whole country, how common A is depends on whose children people are, an (@highlight fam@)d ancestry brings its own diets, habits and diseases.
    draw fam

Keep that warning in mind; first, see what this draw lets us measure.
    highlight share

## From gene to effect
voice: female
level: advanced
sources:
    - id: chen2008
      title: 'Alcohol intake and blood pressure: a systematic review implementing a Mendelian randomization approach'
      authors: Chen, Davey Smith, Harbord and Lewis, PLoS Medicine
      year: 2008
      doi: 10.1371/journal.pmed.0050052
      finding: 'Meta-analysis of five studies (n = 7,658): in men, systolic blood pressure was 7.44 mmHg (95% CI 5.39 to 9.49) higher in ALDH2 *1*1 than in *2*2 homozygotes.'
    - id: millwood2019
      title: 'Conventional and genetic evidence on alcohol and vascular disease aetiology: a prospective study of 500 000 men and women in China'
      authors: Millwood et al. (China Kadoorie Biobank), Lancet
      year: 2019
      doi: 10.1016/S0140-6736(18)31772-0
      finding: 'Self-reported drinking had U-shaped associations with stroke; genotype-predicted male alcohol intake (ALDH2-rs671, ADH1B-rs1229984; 161,498 genotyped) showed no U-shape: ischaemic stroke RR 1.27 (95% CI 1.13 to 1.43) per 280 g/week.'

